| same, direction-estimate error 15 / 30 / 45 deg | {cap:S/controller_qp/15/Fpar_min:0} / {cap:S/controller_qp/30/Fpar_min:0} / {cap:S/controller_qp/45/Fpar_min:0} N | {req:S/controller_qp/15/Fh_max:0} / {req:S/controller_qp/30/Fh_max:0} / {req:S/controller_qp/45/Fh_max:0} N | {qp_err_sf} | {qp_err_lift} N |
| Hybrid (passive floor, controller may only lower) | {cap:S/hybrid/0/Fpar_min:0} N (0 deg error) | {req:S/hybrid/0/Fh_max:0} N | {cap:S/hybrid/0/sf_min:2} | {req:S/hybrid/0/lift_max:0} N |

Passive slip can deviate from the arrest direction by up to {req:S/group_tuned/ang_max:0} deg (perpendicular component up to {req:S/group_tuned/perp_max:0} N).
The worst-case resultant with EVERY cable at its slip tension at once (geometry ignored) is {req:S/group_tuned/upper_bound_all_slip:1} N (≤ {int:K/resultant_bound_all_slip} N) for the
group-tuned set, below the {int:K/envelope_SF1p5} N SF-{desc:R/params/SF:1} envelope, so the bound holds without any direction logic (tested). Sliding SF
at the full slip resultant is >= {cap:S/group_tuned/sf_slide_min:2}. The thresholds are the grid-search optimum (5 N grid, minimum resultant/along
ratio) over the {int:S/group_tuned/n_feasible} triples that meet the three constraints (along >= {int:K/F_lim} N, resultant <= {int:K/envelope_SF1p5} N, lift <= {cap:R/params/CAP_ARREST:0} N); the
earlier 150/150/110 N set (tuned for the narrower 0.11/0.19 belt) gives less than the {int:K/F_lim} N target along the fall with the CAD belt
and was replaced.
Recommendation: passive, group-tuned, spring-applied power-off brakes (guaranteed bound, fail-safe, no controller
in the load path). An electromagnet may trim thresholds per direction, but a current-controlled slip brake alone
is not recommended: it depends on the direction estimate (30 deg error -> {cap:S/controller_qp/30/Fpar_min:0} N, below the {int:K/F_lim} N target) and a
loss of power must still leave a safe bound. Per-spool brake table (r_s = {geo:K/spool_radius*1000:0} mm, rated holding torque = 1.5 x
slip torque, rounded up):

